# camerafrompoints

- Label: Camera from Points
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 21 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/camerafrompoints.html
- Summary (EN): Solves a camera's aspect ratio, focal length, rotation and absolute position from known 3D world points and their matching 2D image projections, using a Perspective-n-Point algorithm with RANSAC to reject outliers. Output named camera. Listed as available since 22.0; the page states this node type is hidden and no longer supported.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud camerafrompoints retrouve la caméra à partir de points 3D connus et de leurs projections 2D, mais la page le déclare masqué et non plus pris en charge.

- Inputs meaning: ["matches: image-world point correspondences, identified by the World and Image Point Attribute parameters", "layer: the layer the solved camera parameters are applied to"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "World Point Attribute / Image Point Attribute", "meaning": "Attributes on matches holding world and image coordinates"}, {"name": "Edit Intrinsics / Focal Length", "meaning": "Enables known intrinsics so the solver does not estimate them"}, {"name": "Camera Center / Image Center / Use Estimator", "meaning": "Projective centre set manually or estimated with an orthocenter estimator; defaults to the image origin"}, {"name": "Parallel Lines / Line A# / Line B#", "meaning": "Axes used by the orthocenter estimator"}, {"name": "RANSAC Seed / Iterations / Tolerance", "meaning": "Random point selection, loop count, reprojection error threshold"}, {"name": "Subset Mode", "meaning": "Percentage or Count of correspondences per candidate; default fixed count of 7"}, {"name": "PnP Reprojection Error", "meaning": "Tolerance used when intrinsics are assumed and there are 3 to 6 correspondences"}, {"name": "Apply Estimated Intrinsics", "meaning": "Writes the solved aspect ratio, aperture and focal length to camera"}]

- Caveats: ["The page states this node type is hidden and no longer supported", "Fewer than 7 correspondences requires known intrinsics; the minimum is 3", "The default centre assumption can give unreliable results where the projective centre is cropped or unknown", "The page title matches; the internal name is not printed on the page, so verify it in Houdini"]

